NNAAMMEE
     iippccrrmm — remove the specified message queues, semaphore sets, and shared
     segments

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iippccrrmm [--WW] [--vv] [--qq _m_s_q_i_d] [--mm _s_h_m_i_d] [--ss _s_e_m_i_d] [--QQ _m_s_g_k_e_y] [--MM _s_h_m_k_e_y]
           [--SS _s_e_m_k_e_y] _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iippccrrmm utility removes the specified message queues, semaphores and
     shared memory segments.  These System V IPC objects can be specified by
     their creation ID or any associated key.

     The following options are generic:

     --vv      If specified once with -W or with -1 for an object, it will show
             all removed objects.  If specified twice with -W or with -1 for
             an objects, it will show all removed objects and all failed re‐
             movals.

     --WW      Try to wipe all specified message queues, semaphores and shared
             memory segments.

     --yy      Use the kvm(3) interface instead of the sysctl(3) interface to
             extract the required information.  If iippccrrmm is to operate on the
             running system, using kvm(3) will require read privileges to
             _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m.

     The following options are used to specify which IPC objects will be re‐
     moved.  Any number and combination of these options can be used:

     --qq _m_s_q_i_d
             Remove the message queue associated with the ID _m_s_q_i_d from the
             system.

     --mm _s_h_m_i_d
             Mark the shared memory segment associated with ID _s_h_m_i_d for re‐
             moval.  This marked segment will be destroyed after the last de‐
             tach.

     --ss _s_e_m_i_d
             Remove the semaphore set associated with ID _s_e_m_i_d from the sys‐
             tem.

     --QQ _m_s_g_k_e_y
             Remove the message queue associated with key _m_s_g_k_e_y from the sys‐
             tem.

     --MM _s_h_m_k_e_y
             Mark the shared memory segment associated with key _s_h_m_k_e_y for re‐
             moval.  This marked segment will be destroyed after the last de‐
             tach.

     --SS _s_e_m_k_e_y
             Remove the semaphore set associated with key _s_e_m_k_e_y from the sys‐
             tem.

     The identifiers and keys associated with these System V IPC objects can
     be determined by using ipcs(1).  If the identifier or the key is -1, it
     will remove all these objects.

